// A replicated value's whole state has to reach a peer as bytes, so a CRDT can only carry data —
// numbers, text, bytes, and lists or maps of them. A value with no wire encoding is refused at the
// call that would have stored it, rather than stored as some shape it would not come back as: a
// register that silently swallowed the difference would look right locally and diverge the moment
// it met a peer.
// expect: error E0007 at 12:5
// expect: exit 1
use para.{crdt}

// A counter is a fine CRDT and a fine *value* — it just is not one this register can send onward.
inner = crdt.gcounter().increment("A", 1)
r = crdt.lww().set("A", inner)
echo r.get() ?? "-"
